fluent-apt-source (2026.10.29-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  The default URI of package repository was changed
  from fluentd.cdn.cncf.io to packages.fluentd.org.

  Why: we want to know how Fluent Package is used, such as which
  distributions, versions and architectures are popular. This helps us
  decide which platforms to support and when to end support for old ones.
  The new URI goes through scarf.sh (https://scarf.sh) to collect download
  statistics, and then redirects your request to the same CDN as before
  (https://fluentd.cdn.cncf.io).

  What is collected: Scarf records metadata derived from your IP
  address, such as coarse location, company and cloud provider.
  It also records the type of client (apt, dnf and so on), basic OS
  information and the requested path. The path shows the
  distribution, version, architecture and package. Scarf discards
  the raw IP address, and we cannot see it. Requests over IPv6 are
  not counted. See the Scarf FAQ and privacy policy for details:
  https://docs.scarf.sh/faq/
  https://about.scarf.sh/privacy-policy/

  Packages and their GPG signatures are not changed. They are still served
  from https://fluentd.cdn.cncf.io.

  If your network limits outgoing access, you may need to allow
  packages.fluentd.org, fluentd.gateway.scarf.sh in addition to
  fluentd.cdn.cncf.io.

  If you do not want to be counted, replace packages.fluentd.org with
  fluentd.cdn.cncf.io in /etc/apt/sources.list.d/fluent.sources.
  Keep the rest of the URI. For example:

    sudo sed -i 's/packages\.fluentd\.org/fluentd.cdn.cncf.io/' \
      /etc/apt/sources.list.d/fluent.sources

  We have no plan to stop serving packages from fluentd.cdn.cncf.io.

 -- Kentaro Hayashi <hayashi@clear-code.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:45:55 +0900
